                        "entry_id": "4340ca98-1a0a-33cb-aa56-84bd4945ed22",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An aluminous earth of a grayish yellow color; a medicinal clay."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8c2bd88-5d4e-49bd-8e97-0440b993c548",
                                "sense_id": "d60f63ee-b55f-3e7a-839c-71e4eb95ff4f",
                                "text": "Dr. Hawks says it is found in Lemnos, sometimes called Terra Lemnia, and used in medicine. It is sometimes called sphragide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10a8c773-b829-4203-8eba-0dc62878d2d0",
                                "sense_id": "d60f63ee-b55f-3e7a-839c-71e4eb95ff4f",
                                "text": "Lemnian earth (sphragide bole, a kind of fine clay)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "246327eb-dac6-4ac3-a341-b1e9c8ce7dda",
                                "sense_id": "d60f63ee-b55f-3e7a-839c-71e4eb95ff4f",
                                "text": "The genuine Lemnian earth of the Greeks, or Sphragide, was a yellowish-grey earth or clay found in the Island of Stalimene (ancient Lemnos)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d450db48-fb53-4e39-999a-6b633404b763",
                                "sense_id": "d60f63ee-b55f-3e7a-839c-71e4eb95ff4f",
                                "text": "Pb content is relatively elevated in the sphragides compared to some of the sediments, but not all (i.e. LE6-1.60)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
